Subject: [PATCH] Present: a run of failed presents, or pictures that stop moving on, go back to GL's swap (TODO 362)

A player's fresh install showed only a black window with the game and its sound running, F1's menu missing too (it
is drawn into the same pictures). The DXGI hand-over's failures that left it so were only counted: the interop's lock
refused on every picture, the swap chain's back buffer or present failing (a lost presenting device), a GL fence or
the read guard's query that never passes (the window's thread then crawled at a picture each 250 ms), the window's
render texture that could not be made. Now: each kind's first failure is said with its code; half a second of them
in a row (30), or pictures handed over that have not moved on for 5 s, or 30 pictures without a render texture, send
the window to GL's own swap with the existing "GL's own swap from now on" line; 10 s after the start with nothing
shown a line names the stage reached; two graphics chips (the window's screen on one, GL on another) are said at the
start; and a picture check (each picture until it knows, nothing presented before it - a window that has once shown
a flip-model swap chain's picture shows GL's own swap no more, black on both Intel laptops: two all-but-black marks drawn last into the window's picture,
looked for in the window's own picture and in Direct3D's copy) sends it to GL's swap where they do not arrive - the
ThinkPad's UHD 620 with the legacy-handle textures: every present succeeded, the window was black. close() no longer waits without end for a present thread held inside a driver's call. Test switches:
PS2X_PRESENT_FAULT=lock|present|fence|target forces each failure; PS2X_PRESENT_FALLBACK=0 keeps the swap chain
whatever fails (as before); PS2X_PRESENT_CHECK=0 no picture check. Healthy machines: nothing changes but the counts.

